lines=['# Smaller Stream1090 RF windows — Pi comparison','', '**Shorter independent decoder processes reduce candidate-ready delay but lose unique packets and use more CPU. Keep the working one-second version. Production is unchanged.**','', 'The same 24 historical RF seconds were decoded on Mac and Pi. All Stream1090 packet bytes and timestamps match exactly across architectures for every tested variant. The full currently enabled DSP/neural union was recomputed on the Pi with copies of its actual native/Rust libraries, three neural models, method and worker configuration. SIC/header remain off; Broad CRC remains quarantined. Stock, historical actual relay and available accepted-production records mask discoveries.','', '| RF core / calibration | Stream-only extras beyond other current methods | Lost from full current union | New beyond current | Median candidate-ready age | Stream CPU change |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
