lines+=['', 'The current complete DSP union has 403 extras; 34 depend uniquely on Stream1090. With the best shortened policies, the union falls to 393 (500 ms), 380 (250 ms) and 374 (rolling 100 ms). There are no new packets beyond either the recomputed current union or recorded actual output. The shorter variants retain 24/34, 11/34 and 5/34 Stream-only extras respectively. Losses refer to replacement by the shortened version, after every other enabled method has a chance to cover the packet. Stock output itself is not replaced or lost.', '', 'Latency values are measured **Stream1090 candidate-ready RF age**, under the isolated Pi replay quota—not final admission, relay or FR24 cloud latency. Inputs are paced at native RF speed. Recorded stock arrival wall times are unavailable, so alignment stock context is assumed available at clip close. Medians are conditional on surviving extras; low latency obtained by discarding packets is not a throughput improvement. For the same retained packets, median saved time was 483 ms at 500 ms, 780 ms at 250 ms and 950 ms at rolling 100 ms. The rolling-100-ms latency sample contains only five Stream-only packets.', '', '## CPU cost', '', '| RF core | Stream child CPU s / RF s | Change | Full decoder-kernel bundle CPU change |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
